<%# One pending follow-request row in the inbox (2026 follow gaps). Local: `follow`
    (a pending passive Follow). Structure mirrors users/_user_row's identity block —
    40px `ui/_avatar`, medium name, faint `@handle` — but the action buttons are
    SIBLINGS of the profile link, never nested inside the `<a>` (a button inside an
    anchor is invalid HTML). The identity link takes `flex-1`.

    `border-b border-gray-100` is the design system's #f3f4f6 hairline: unlike the
    `<a>`-rooted _user_row (whose bare `border-b` picks up the base layer's `--fg-link`
    on links), this row is a `<div>`, but the colour is still stated explicitly so the
    separator never inherits `currentColor`.

    Accept/decline are the exact notification-card idiom
    (_notification_card.html.erb) — bare `ds_button_classes(variant: :link)` controls,
    not solid pills. They post to /follow_requests/:id (FollowRequestPolicy gates them
    to this user). The responses are turbo_stream: accept/decline remove this row in
    place (_actioned.turbo_stream.erb removes `dom_id(follow, :request)`) with an HTML
    fallback that `redirect_back`s for no-JS clients. %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(follow, :request) %>" class="flex items-center gap-3 p-3 bg-card border-b border-gray-100">
  <%= link_to profile_path(follow.follower.username),
        class: "flex-1 flex items-center gap-3 no-underline min-w-0" do %>
    <%= render "ui/avatar", user: follow.follower, size: :row %>
    <div class="flex flex-col min-w-0">
      <span class="font-medium truncate"><%= follow.follower.full_name %></span>
      <span class="text-sm text-light-grey truncate">@<%= follow.follower.username %></span>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div class="flex items-center gap-3 shrink-0">
    <%= button_to "Accept", follow_request_path(follow), method: :patch,
          class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link) %>
    <%= button_to "Decline", follow_request_path(follow), method: :delete,
          class: ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>
  </div>
</div>
